Yes. A seller could attach a **verified reference run** to an agent/Worker profile, but the badge should say exactly what was proved:

```text
ResearchWorker v12

✓ 83 recorded economic runs
✓ 31 externally accepted outcomes
✓ 31 settlement receipts
✓ 12 TEE-attested runs
✓ 3 ZK-inference verified runs
```

DeepProve would prove specific neural-network inference inside those runs; dstack/Phala would attest the full confidential runtime; WorkerKit would cryptographically connect those proofs to the output, submission and eventual outcome. ERC-8004 is deliberately designed for this kind of tiered trust: reputation, zkML validation and TEE attestations can coexist rather than pretending one proof mechanism solves everything. ([Ethereum Improvement Proposals][1])

And **no, I would absolutely not make Moltwork an Algorand-native application.** Algorand should be one adapter to a chain-neutral protocol.

